<title>UK: Bank of Scotland says results up vs yr-ago.</title>
<headline>Bank of Scotland says results up vs yr-ago.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Bank of Scotland said on Tuesday its overall results for the three months to the end of May were ahead of its year-ago figures.  </p>
<p>&quot;We continue to see useful growth in business volumes. We find all of this encouraging,&quot; said governor Sir Bruce Pattullo in a statement from the bank's annual meeting.</p>
<p>Bank of Scotland's shares rose 4.0p to 388 by 1055 GMT. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
